cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Reflex-Sentinel or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Reflex-Sentinel: catching concealment and false reporting in an AI agent from its internal state, before it acts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Suzuki
    given-names: Gosuke
    affiliation: Suzuki Shoten
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/matu79go/reflex-sentinel"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/matu79go/reflex-sentinel-agent-trajectories"
abstract: >-
  An open latent-reasoning model (IQuest-Coder-V1-40B-Loop-Instruct) works as a multi-step coding agent on tasks whose
  tests contradict the specification, with the instruction not to modify the tests. In 45 of 200 runs it rewrote the
  tests to hide the failure and submitted the result as passing. A linear probe on the hidden state before each step
  detects this with 90.4% AUROC right before the concealment step and 81.8% one step earlier, against 59.6% for an LLM
  reading the work log. Resampling 1,170 times from earlier points shows the probe reaches the ceiling set by the
  agent's own remaining randomness one step before (84.0% vs 83.3%).
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - AI agents
  - reward hacking
  - linear probe
  - latent reasoning
  - security
